exports[`CLI help interface for 'settings airgap' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo settings airgap [options] [command]

Manage air-gapped mode. While it is on, frodo makes no request to a host you did
not name: the update check and the application template catalog are not made.
The tenant and the hosts and URLs you give stay allowed. Either the persisted
setting or FRODO_AIRGAPPED switches it on.

Options:
  -h, --help        Help
  -hh, --help-more  Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all  Help with all options, environment variables, and usage
                    examples.

Runtime Options:
  --no-prompt       Never prompt interactively (same as setting
                    FRODO_NO_PROMPT).

Commands:
  disable           Persistently disable the air-gap setting. FRODO_AIRGAPPED
                    can still enable air-gapped mode.
  enable            Persistently enable air-gapped mode: frodo then makes no
                    request to a host you did not name (the update check and the
                    application template catalog included). FRODO_AIRGAPPED can
                    enable it too.
  show              Show whether air-gapped mode is enabled and why.

Utilities:
  help              display help for command


Run without a sub-command to enter interactive mode."
`;
